  SW->>N: Install Swamp<br/>cfgmgmt fetch
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the recipe's pinned Swamp release by SHA-256 at `/usr/local/lib/orbit-swamp/<version>/swamp`, a path no process runs from yet
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Keep the running Swamp<br/>SSH argv
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - while `/usr/local/bin/swamp` is still a file, renames it into a new directory under `/usr/local/lib/orbit-swamp` and links the path to the release at once; a rename keeps the inode, so a running serve or worker keeps a binary it can start children from
  %%> Why:
  %%> - replacing the file in place left the running workers on a deleted binary, and every 209 dispatch failed until they restarted
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Link Swamp<br/>cfgmgmt link
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - points `/usr/local/bin/swamp`, which serve and the workers run, at the pinned release; a running process keeps the file it started from, and the new release takes effect at its next restart
  end
